msherman@sybase.com (Marc Sherman) writes:

>Spoil me, please!  If I have a scroll that I like (say, Identify), a
>spellbook of blank paper, and a magic marker, is there any way that I
>can make a spellbook of identify?


Apply the magic marker to the blank scroll or spellbook. Write
"identify" (not the words that are on a scroll of identify). The magic
marker must have enough charges left (some scrolls are more expensive
in charges than others).

This only works if you have identified the scroll or spellbook that you
wish to write (I'm not usre what you meant exactly with "I have a
scroll I like": do you have that scroll or did you mean "there is a
scroll I like"?).

If you've NOT already identified the scroll you wish to write, then you
only have a 1 in 15 chance of succes. If you are playing a wizard, the
chance is 1 in 3. Once you are succesful, you have automatically
identified the scroll or spellbook, so from then on, you can write it
without problems.

